{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-66628",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $0.01$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n0.01={10}^{-2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.01)=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{-2})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=-2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{-2})=-2\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
